cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ForkUnion: NUMA-Aware Fork-Join with No Allocations, Syscalls or CAS Loops, Parking Workers on Address Monitors"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/ashvardanian/ForkUnion
url: https://github.com/ashvardanian/ForkUnion
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21472185
abstract: >-
  ForkUnion is a NUMA-aware fork-join thread-pool for systems languages, built for the tightest
  parallel-for loops rather than task queues. Its dispatch hot path makes no heap allocations and no
  system calls and no compare-and-swap loops, and shares no cache line between workers, so
  fork-join latency stays flat as cores and sockets multiply. Idle
  workers park on a hardware address monitor where the processor offers one, waking the instant a
  peer writes the watched cache line, while per-domain memory placement and private per-worker
  cursors keep synchronization off the interconnect.
keywords:
  - numa
  - parallel
  - thread pool
  - fork-join
  - allocator

authors:
